public enum IdnaError {
  Invalid();
  TooLarge();
}

public fn domain_to_ascii(domain: &[u32], output: &Box<Slots<u8>>) -> result: Result<unit, IdnaError> reads(domain), writes(output) contract {
  requires domain^.len <= 16777216_u64;
} doc "Appends the result of ToASCII of Unicode Technical Standard #46 for Unicode 17.0.0 on domain to output, after output's existing contents, with the flags the URL Standard's domain parser ToASCII sets when beStrict is false: UseSTD3ASCIIRules false, CheckHyphens false, CheckBidi true, CheckJoiners true, Transitional_Processing false, VerifyDnsLength false and IgnoreInvalidPunycode false. Mapping, validity and the Bidi and joiner checks use that version's IdnaMappingTable.txt and character database: DerivedBidiClass.txt, DerivedJoiningType.txt, DerivedGeneralCategory.txt and the canonical combining classes of UnicodeData.txt, with normalization from pkg::text::normalization. Invalid when processing records an error that these flags do not ignore; a value in domain that is not a Unicode scalar value is disallowed. Output then holds exactly its prior contents, and does too on TooLarge, when output would pass its storage limit.";
